WEBVTT

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:17.560
Hey, Mom, guess what. 
I learned a new song the other day!

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.870
Then why don't you sing it 
for me after breakfast?

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:21.880
Okay!

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:26.580
<i>I guess this isn't a dream after all.</i>

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:31.920
Sunday, May 13th 2018 (Heisei 30)

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:31.920
<i>When I woke up this morning, 
I found myself in the year 2018.</i>

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:36.390
<i>And I'm not sure how, 
but I'm married to Shinoaki,</i>

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:39.320
<i>and we have a daughter named Maki.</i>

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.930
<i>Naturally, I have no memory 
of anything in between.</i>

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:47.360
<i>It was weird enough that
 I leaped ten years back</i>

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:49.590
<i>when I was originally from 2016...</i>

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:52.230
<i>But why am I in 2018 now?</i>

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.030
<i>Plus, this situation...</i>

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:56.910
Honey!

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.210
Uh, wh-what is it?

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:00.500
What's wrong?

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.600
You've been chewing on that toast 
since breakfast started.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.380
Daddy, no fair!

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:09.710
You always say I have to eat everything, 
instead of just my favorites!

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.710
You're right!

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:14.880
It's important to have a balanced diet, huh?

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:18.920
<i>So now I'm a dad all of a sudden, huh?</i>

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:21.470
<i>It doesn't feel real at all.</i>

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:25.430
Sunday, May 13th 2018 (Heisei 30)

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:25.430
<i>But for now, I need to confirm 
what's going on around me.</i>

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:31.530
<i>It looks like we currently 
live in Noborito, not Osaka.</i>

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:34.440
<i>It's a town between the prefectures 
of Kanagawa and Tokyo.</i>

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.590
<i>And after graduating from Oonaka Arts,</i>

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:41.240
<i>I've been working at a game 
company called Attraction Point.</i>

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:45.970
<i>I hope there's someone 
I can talk to in here.</i>

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:51.130
<b>April 14th, 2018</b>

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:51.130
<b>Kawasegawa Eiko</b>

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:51.130
<b></b>Call

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:48.910
<i>Last contact was a month ago.</i>

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:51.130
<i>No idea what our relationship is, but...</i>

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:55.090
<i>Hello?</i>

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:57.000
Hey, Kawasegawa?

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.370
I'm not sure if it's been a while...

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:01.010
<i>Perfect timing.</i>

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:03.070
<i>Remember what I told you about last month?</i>

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:04.890
<i>It's gone as poorly as I thought.</i>

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:06.950
U-Uh, actually, Kawasegawa—

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:09.150
<i>Can you come in a little early tomorrow?</i>

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.950
<i>About 30 minutes before you're scheduled?</i>

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:13.910
<i>I'll have one of my people 
come get you. See you then.</i>

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:15.640
Uh, Kawasegawa?

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:20.410
But I'm the one who wanted to 
ask <i>her</i> for help.

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:25.330
<b>Development Department
Entertainment Group Section 3
Development Manager</b>

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:25.330
<i>I guess I'm working at the same company 
as Kawasegawa in this world, too.</i>

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:28.330
<i>That's at least something to go on.</i>

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:31.260
<i>It's like one step forward.</i>

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.470
Okay, okay...

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:06.760
May 14th (Monday) 2018

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:06.890
May 14th (Monday) 2018

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:08.810
May 14th (Monday) 2018

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:14.240
<i>I was kinda hoping I'd open my eyes 
and be back in 2007.</i>

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:15.920
<i>But no such luck.</i>

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:19.620
<i>Being married all of a sudden...</i>

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:41.450
What?

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:43.450
Oh, it's nothing!

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:45.130
Good morning, Mommy!

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:46.140
Good morning.

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:47.720
Good morning, Daddy!

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:51.570
Yeah. Good morning, Maki.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:53.770
Here's your lunch!

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:56.220
Okay. Thanks.

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:57.230
Well...

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.650
Have a good day!

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:03.440
Right! I'm off.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.960
<i>That said...</i>

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:10.200
<i>The fact that I have no memory of this life 
means it'll be easy to screw something up.</i>

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:12.730
<i>Will I be able to pull this off?</i>

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:24.760
<i>Were crowded trains always this packed?</i>

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:28.660
<i>Attraction Point was a famous game company</i>

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:31.970
<i>in the 2016 I originally came from, too.</i>

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:34.350
<i>They weren't considered 
the top of the industry,</i>

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:38.190
<i>but they managed to turn out hits at a regular 
enough pace... a solid, mid-tier developer.</i>

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:41.500
<i>This is it.</i>

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:51.910
<i>What exactly does "Development Manager 
of Entertainment Group Section 3" even do?</i>

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:54.240
Good morn—

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:58.710
<i>Maybe I shouldn't have taken Sunday off?</i>

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:05.700
Uh, my desk is...

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:08.620
Oh, there it is.

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:11.430
Hashiba-san!

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:14.650
Excuse me! The producer wants to—

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:18.250
Are you okay?

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:20.370
Yes!

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:22.060
<b>Development Department
Entertainment Group Section 3</b>

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:24.320
<i>Morishita Miki...</i>

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:27.680
<i>She must be who Kawasegawa mentioned.</i>

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:29.820
Can you come with me to Tahiti right now?

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:30.880
Okay.

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:32.950
<i>Wait, Tahiti?!</i>

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:36.380
<i>Oh, that's what she meant.</i>

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:38.130
Here he is!

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:39.870
Thank you. Come on in.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.910
Pardon us.

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:47.760
Sorry to drag you in so early.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:52.420
What's wrong? You're staring a little.

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:55.950
Oh, uh, it's nothing.

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:57.850
So, what did you need?

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:00.060
I am so sorry...

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:03.240
This is really something our team 
should be dealing with.

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:05.620
But here you are, taking care of it.

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:06.990
You don't need to worry about it.

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:08.650
Thank you so much.

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:11.650
The producer was right about you!

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:13.620
Did Kawasegawa mention me before?

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:17.250
Yes! "If we let Hashiba-san 
handle it, it'll be fine."

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:20.120
"Since he was a student, 
he's had secret tricks"

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:22.710
"that'll help turn around even 
the most dire situations!"

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:27.000
As glad as I am to have her faith, 
it feels kinda exaggerated.

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:30.590
<i>Yes?</i>

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:32.950
This is Hashiba, from Attraction Point.

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:35.080
<i>Oh, I was waiting for you!</i>

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:36.600
<i>I'll buzz you in.</i>

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.470
No way!

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:42.480
You really are amazing, Hashiba-san.

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:46.070
Every time I tried to get ahold of her, 
she pretended she wasn't home.

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:48.950
This must be one of those 
tricks I heard about!

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:50.850
It's nothing fancy like that.

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:53.840
First, I used social media 
to confirm that she was home.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:57.320
Then, 30 minutes before we 
got here, I sent this message.

00:07:57.320 --> 00:08:00.820
"I'm in your neighborhood right now, Sensei."

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:03.290
"Is it all right if I come by?"

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:06.360
I get it! It'd be hard to say no 
to something like that.

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:08.550
But why 30 minutes beforehand?

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:12.550
Well, if she wants to do her makeup, 
or clean up the room...

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:15.070
It gives the other party time to prepare.

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:19.040
That goes for getting mentally prepared, too.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:22.300
You have a much better chance 
of meeting with someone

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:23.790
if you give them a little buffer.

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:25.150
I see!

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:28.930
I'm just glad that was all I had to do.

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:29.940
What do you mean?

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:32.860
Well, it's nothing illegal.

00:08:33.230 --> 00:08:36.300
But there are more devious tactics.

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:46.630
Coming!

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:48.290
Sorry about the delay—

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:49.250
Hello!

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:53.340
It's good to see you again, Sensei.

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:55.700
Look...

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:59.810
Um... I didn't mean to cause any problems.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:03.720
But y'know, there are times when 
it's hard to get anything done, right?

00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:05.040
You can try to draw something

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:06.690
but it turns out, like, 
"What the heck is this?"

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:08.180
<i>Minori Ayaka.</i>

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:10.310
<i>Her real name is Saikawa Minori.</i>

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:14.400
<i>She's a particularly popular illustrator 
who's got over 200,000 followers.</i>

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:19.990
<i>She's handling the main 
character designs on a project</i>

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:22.930
<i>that Attraction Point has 
staked its entire future on.</i>

00:09:23.590 --> 00:09:27.020
<i>And with one of the most popular 
illustrators in the zeitgeist working on it,</i>

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:29.410
<i>the game's profile is nice and high.</i>

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:31.550
<i>Which is a start, but...</i>

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:35.270
I understand! Believe me, I understand.

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:37.720
I seriously, just honestly 
can't get anything done!

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:38.550
But...

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:43.820
<i>It seems that Minori Ayaka
 isn't the quickest worker.</i>

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:44.870
Sensei...

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:48.950
The designs were scheduled 
to be finished by February.

00:09:48.950 --> 00:09:53.340
You've never needed this much 
extra time before, correct?

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:56.410
For you to be at a standstill 
at a time like this...

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:58.550
I'm guessing there's 
some sort of reason why.

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:01.840
Something that goes beyond 
just not being motivated.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:07.450
There really is no fooling you, 
huh, Hashiba-san?

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:14.760
There's just... nothing 
I want to draw anymore.

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:17.920
Do you mean...

00:10:18.310 --> 00:10:20.940
I've done everything I wanted to.

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:23.100
So I'm thinking... maybe that's enough.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:27.800
B-But... you have so many fans, Sensei!

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:30.720
Well, of course I'm grateful to my fans.

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:34.770
But that doesn't have anything to do 
with the desire to draw.

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:38.010
It feels like there's nothing 
to get excited about.

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:40.530
Or like I'm not sure what 
I'm working toward anymore.

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:42.980
Oh, no...

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:44.660
Hashiba-san!

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:47.140
Hashiba-san?

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:49.670
That art...

00:10:50.270 --> 00:10:53.520
Wait! That's still a work-in-progress!

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:59.700
This is incredible.

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:02.570
It's a wonderful piece of art.

00:11:02.570 --> 00:11:05.080
It seems different 
from your usual style, too.

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:08.310
But it feels natural, like you've 
been drawing this way for years.

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:11.790
And the style you're using 
is a perfect match for the subject.

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:13.690
It's honestly overwhelming!

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:18.760
That is <i>so</i> great to hear!

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:22.380
Do you really, really like it, Hashiba-san?!

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:23.740
Yes. A great deal.

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:25.600
Awesome!

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:26.980
See, this piece...

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:30.320
I drew it using a style closer 
to what I started out with!

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:32.080
I was trying to get back to my roots!

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:33.580
Back to your roots?

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:36.840
Yeah! There's an artist I used to idolize,

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:39.260
and this is their style.

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:42.590
I seriously, seriously love their stuff!

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:47.480
I think I'm feeling kinda motivated now!

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:49.470
Really?!

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:51.910
I mean, I can't promise 
anything right away...

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:55.780
But I'm feeling more optimistic 
about getting things done, maybe?

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:59.860
For now, let's hear about 
the schedule you mentioned.

00:12:00.830 --> 00:12:01.820
Of course!

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:07.030
<i>I wasn't sure how this would go, 
but it seems to have worked out.</i>

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:10.490
<i>It's different from the future I wanted.</i>

00:12:10.490 --> 00:12:12.620
<i>But it looks like there's something 
for me to do in this world, too.</i>

00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:16.630
<i>I'm able to work with 
talented creators like her.</i>

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:20.240
<i>I guess my dream came true, 
one way or another.</i>

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:21.450
Okay!

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:26.730
Come on, Maki, eat your vegetables.

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:31.520
<i>This is probably most 
people's idea of happiness.</i>

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:35.240
<i>A cute wife, our daughter,</i>

00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:37.060
<i>and a job that's going well...</i>

00:12:37.970 --> 00:12:38.980
Honey?

00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:41.710
You seem happy.

00:12:41.710 --> 00:12:43.880
Did something good happen at work?

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:46.540
Well, yeah.

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:49.740
I actually got to meet 
Minori Ayaka-san today.

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:52.860
Minori... Ayaka-san?

00:12:52.860 --> 00:12:56.280
She's a famous illustrator. 
Have you not heard of her?

00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:59.670
No... sorry.

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:05.180
Come to think of it, Summer Comiket 
is taking submissions soon.

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:06.760
Did you apply?

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:10.290
Honey...

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:12.760
Kyoya-kun, what are you talking about?

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:17.220
I haven't drawn in years.

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:23.610
Wh-Why?!

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:25.100
Daddy?

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:35.290
There was... nothing 
I wanted to draw anymore.

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:39.880
There's just... nothing 
I want to draw anymore.

00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:43.790
Honey? Honey!

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:46.240
Are you okay?

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:49.090
Oh... yeah.

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:51.830
Daddy, that's bad manners!

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:53.220
It's okay, Maki.

00:13:53.630 --> 00:13:56.480
Dad's just kind of surprised.

00:13:56.480 --> 00:13:58.450
Surprised? About what?

00:13:58.450 --> 00:13:59.480
<i>Shinoaki...</i>

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:03.800
<i>Akishima Shino has stopped making art?</i>

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:08.690
<i>That's... That can't be.</i>

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:19.210
Hashiba-kun, this isn't gonna cut it!

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:22.800
I need you to convince her to actually 
get back to work like usual!

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:25.860
But president, thanks to 
Hashiba-san, the schedule—

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:27.970
I need more than just a schedule!

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:30.000
We can't even get started

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.220
if she doesn't get some 
of these designs done!

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:36.540
I'm asking you to do this because you 
usually manage to get things taken care of.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:40.090
Try and take care of Minori Ayaka 
as soon as possible, all right?

00:14:41.450 --> 00:14:43.060
I'm sorry...

00:14:43.340 --> 00:14:47.370
This was our team's problem, 
and you're taking the blame for it.

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:49.960
It's okay. It's not a big deal.

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:53.450
By the way, do you want to 
grab lunch with me?

00:14:54.810 --> 00:14:56.630
This sucks.

00:14:56.630 --> 00:15:00.040
I would've given the president 
a piece of my mind in the old days.

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:02.380
I've been totally defanged.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:03.730
It's not like that.

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:07.500
Once you've got a position like producer, 
you can't act as hastily.

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:09.770
You haven't changed, Kawasegawa.

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:11.030
You think so?

00:15:11.030 --> 00:15:11.860
Yeah.

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:13.360
Even your lunch...

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:16.850
It's got a good nutritional balance, 
and is nice and varied.

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:19.130
You're busy, but you still mind the details.

00:15:19.130 --> 00:15:22.460
Come on. I just threw something together.

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:26.400
But look at you. Every day 
you eat a specially-made lunch.

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:28.670
Yeah.

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:35.160
I have to say, the idea of Shinoaki 
getting up every morning to make lunch...

00:15:35.670 --> 00:15:38.750
I couldn't have imagined that
back when we were students.

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:40.410
You're right about that.

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:43.450
She was always so awkward, and had 
trouble with laundry and cleaning,

00:15:43.450 --> 00:15:45.090
not to mention cooking.

00:15:47.700 --> 00:15:50.280
<i>In the eleven years I wasn't privy to,</i>

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:53.390
<i>Shinoaki gave up on becoming Akishima Shino,</i>

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:55.260
<i>and became my wife instead.</i>

00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:58.910
<i>Then there's Kawasegawa...</i>

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:03.400
I'm the head of SucceedSoft's 
second development group, Kawasegawa.

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:04.270
Nice to have you.

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:08.030
<i>She used to work at 
the industry leader, Succeed.</i>

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:10.290
<i>And in a higher position 
than she has now, too.</i>

00:16:10.290 --> 00:16:12.970
Okay, understood. I'll be back soon.

00:16:14.310 --> 00:16:18.260
Sorry, there's something 
that needs a response ASAP.

00:16:19.230 --> 00:16:21.210
I'm going to have to cut out early.

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:22.410
Oh, okay.

00:16:25.780 --> 00:16:28.880
<i>These changes have to 
be the result of my enrollment</i>

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:31.550
<i>into Oonaka University for the Arts in 2006.</i>

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:33.090
<i>There's no other explanation.</i>

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:37.990
<i>If this entire world is an extension 
of what happened back then...</i>

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:41.100
<b>Followers:</b>

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:43.350
<i>Are you kidding me?!</i>

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.440
<b>Important Announcement</b>

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.440
<b>An important announcement (Streaming...)</b>

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.440
<b>Uploaded 13:05 05/14/2018</b>

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.440
<b>What is it? What's going on?</b>

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.440
<b>361 Views</b>

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.440
<b>Comments:</b>

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.440
<b>Background music for work collection</b>

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.440
<b>Uploaded 20:00 04/18/2018</b>

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:54.200
<i>Well, I'm afraid I've got 
some bad news today.</i>

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:58.910
<i>This is going to be my last stream.</i>

00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:03.210
<i>I'm sorry to everyone who's 
listened to me for all this time.</i>

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:07.500
<i>It just feels like I'm not sure what 
I'm singing for anymore, you know?</i>

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:11.840
<i>That being the case, 
I hope you enjoy my final song!</i>

00:17:16.280 --> 00:17:19.300
<i>This can't... be happening.</i>

00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:21.490
<i>Even Nanako?</i>

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:27.400
<b>Kawagoe</b>

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:27.400
<b>Kyoichi</b>

00:17:30.950 --> 00:17:32.260
Nothing!

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:33.530
<i>Then maybe...</i>

00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:35.280
<b>Rokuonji</b>

00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:35.280
<b>Tsurayuki</b>

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:40.870
<b><u>From the Desk of Tsurayuki Rokuonji</u></b>

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:42.880
<i>He hasn't written any novels?!</i>

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:44.670
<i>Tsurayuki...</i>

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:47.460
<b>Spring Brings a New Wind

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:51.750
<i>It was me.</i>

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:55.220
I'm dropping out of school.

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:57.840
<i>Because of me...</i>

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:03.160
I realized how I couldn't 
accomplish anything without you.

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:04.850
"I can't stay here."

00:18:05.720 --> 00:18:08.620
<i>Because of me... they're all...</i>

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:23.660
<i>I wanted to remake my life.</i>

00:18:24.230 --> 00:18:26.860
<i>Into the ideal future I had dreamed of...</i>

00:18:27.350 --> 00:18:31.710
<i>I thought I would do everything 
I could to make that happen.</i>

00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:35.600
<i>With special friends, 
who had special talents...</i>

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:39.550
<i>I wanted to get close 
to the brilliance of the people</i>

00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:41.550
<i>who would be called 
the Platinum Generation...</i>

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:48.390
<i>But... what I ended up doing 
is stealing their dreams,</i>

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:52.810
<i>creating a world where 
I'm the only one who's happy.</i>

00:18:58.090 --> 00:19:01.510
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:05.240
I'm home.

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:09.340
What happened?! You're a total mess!

00:19:09.340 --> 00:19:12.080
Daddy, you stink like booze!

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:13.150
Sorry.

00:19:13.780 --> 00:19:15.920
I'm sorry, Shinoaki.

00:19:17.600 --> 00:19:19.180
It's okay.

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:22.010
Something real bad must've happened, huh?

00:19:22.860 --> 00:19:24.090
I'm sorry!

00:19:24.090 --> 00:19:25.900
I mean it, I'm sorry!

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:27.640
It's my fault!

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:30.650
Because of me, you...

00:19:30.650 --> 00:19:31.880
Kyoya-kun...

00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:34.720
Oh, no, Daddy's crying!

00:19:34.720 --> 00:19:36.110
Like a kid.

00:19:46.530 --> 00:19:51.620
I kinda figured you'd gotten 
over it by now...

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:55.130
Me not drawing anymore.

00:19:56.330 --> 00:19:57.880
Shinoaki...

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:03.440
I never did tell you why, huh?

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:06.360
It must've been troubling you all this time.

00:20:08.790 --> 00:20:10.560
HaruSora sold well...

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:15.410
And even without Tsurayuki-kun, 
we kept on making games.

00:20:15.410 --> 00:20:18.020
Remember how it went?

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:22.080
I guess I do...

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:27.740
But at some point, I wasn't even sure 
if what I was doing was art anymore.

00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:33.620
<i>Because I was in a rush 
to finish the game,</i>

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:37.600
<i>I ended up snuffing out Shinoaki's 
individuality as a creator</i>

00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:39.170
<i>to suit my own priorities.</i>

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:43.180
<i>If that turned into a pattern afterward...</i>

00:20:43.830 --> 00:20:47.840
I may have done something 
there's no coming back from.

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:53.860
It started being less and less fun to draw.

00:20:53.860 --> 00:20:58.340
But you were just trying 
to do what you could.

00:20:58.340 --> 00:21:00.580
You worked harder than anyone!

00:21:00.580 --> 00:21:03.490
So it ain't your fault, you hear?

00:21:04.590 --> 00:21:05.820
It's more that...

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:10.950
I would feel bad about what I was making, 
when no one was around.

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:13.170
What do you mean?

00:21:13.170 --> 00:21:16.710
I'd make art, and you 
would always praise it.

00:21:17.060 --> 00:21:21.600
When I put it out into the world, 
even more folks would say it was good.

00:21:21.600 --> 00:21:25.750
Even when I wasn't satisfied with it... 
and didn't know what I was doing.

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:30.470
It started to really scare me.

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:36.240
<i>She must've been feeling a kind of solitude</i>

00:21:36.240 --> 00:21:38.320
<i>that only she could understand back then.</i>

00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:45.040
<i>And I wasn't able to realize it.</i>

00:21:50.420 --> 00:21:51.990
It's okay now.

00:21:55.460 --> 00:21:56.630
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:03.270
<i>Shinoaki... I'm so sorry.</i>
